# $app_name

A simple search app over the graph `$graph_name`, generated by lakebase-graph-kit. It serves
one walk (web, depth $depth, top $top_n per hop) through the served views in
`$served_schema`, as the Postgres role `reader`. The kit does not deploy it; you deploy it with
your own permissions.

## Before the first deploy (once)

1. Create the app in the workspace (UI or `databricks apps create $app_name`).
2. Give the app's service principal a Lakebase login that can become `reader`. In the branch
   Postgres, as the project owner:

   ```sql
   CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS databricks_auth;
   SELECT databricks_create_role('<app service principal client id>', 'service_principal');
   GRANT CONNECT ON DATABASE databricks_postgres TO "<app service principal client id>";
   GRANT reader TO "<app service principal client id>";
   ```

   Grant the service principal nothing else. It reads only as `reader`.
3. Grant the service principal `CAN_USE` on the Lakebase project `$lakebase_project`.
4. Copy this folder to the workspace path the deploy command uses:
   `$workspace_path` (for example with `databricks sync`).

## Deploy

The kit printed this command:

```
$deploy_command
```

## What the app reads

See `DATA_CONTRACT.md`. The app reads only `$served_schema.nodes_view`,
`$served_schema.edges_view` and `$served_schema.node_id_map_view`. The `reader` role cannot read
the raw version tables.
